    "title": "Channing Tatum's sparkly thong crashes Robert Downey Jr., Chris Evans Oscars reunion",
    "text": "Updated March 15, 2026, 9:54 p.m. ETOscar presenters, assemble!Marvel stars Robert Downey Jr. and Chris Evans reunited at the Oscars on Sunday, where they marked the 14th anniversary of the original \"Avengers\" movie and presented the awards for best screenplay.In a playful bit on stage, Evans asked Downey what he got him as an anniversary gift.\"It's the 14th year anniversary of our first 'Avengers' movie,\" Evans said. \"I got you a signed copy of the original script, signed by the whole cast. It's backstage. See, I really thought this through!\"Downey scrambled in the bit as it became clear that he did not have a gift prepared, and the pair quickly transitioned into giving out the Oscar for adapted screenplay.After Paul Thomas Anderson accepted the award for \"One Battle After Another,\" Evans returned to the stage by himself. It initially seemed like Downey had abandoned him, only for the \"Iron Man\" star to rush back to present his costar with an anniversary gift.\"I was just joshing. Of course, I got you something,\" Downey told Evans, before pulling out a sparkly thong that he explained was used by Channing Tatum on \"Magic Mike.\"The capper? Tatum himself was in the audience.\"I'm gonna need that back, though!\" he shouted from his seat, noting, \"I've got to work later!\"Downey and Evans have been longtime Marvel costars going back to 2012's \"The Avengers,\" which united their superheroes Iron Man and Captain America. In 2019, \"Avengers: Endgame\" served as a farewell to both characters, with Downey's Iron Man dying and Evans' Captain America retiring.But the Oscars reunion comes as both actors are set to return to the Marvel universe later this year in \"Avengers: Doomsday.\" Evans is reprising his role of Steve Rogers, while Downey will take on a new character: Doctor Doom, the main villain of the film.Evans and Downey weren't the only Marvel actors in attendance at the Oscars. Downey's longtime \"Iron Man\" costar Gwyneth Paltrow, who played Tony Stark's love interest Pepper Potts, helped present the Oscar for best casting. She is part of the cast of the film \"Marty Supreme.\"Tatum also stars with Evans and Downey in \"Avengers: Doomsday,\" reprising his role of Gambit from \"Deadpool & Wolverine.\"",
